 "tariffNote": "CALENDAR years, NIPA (accrual) basis. Effective rate computed by us = duties / goods imports. The annual NIPA series match the average of the quarterly SAAR values to within rounding in every year 1959-2025 (checked). 2026 = average of the two quarters available (Q1 326.223 and Q2 306.398 SAAR for duties; Q1 3439.879 and Q2 3727.887 SAAR for goods imports), i.e., an annualized first-half rate. IMPORTANT for 2025-2026: on 2026-02-20 the Supreme Court held in Learning Resources, Inc. v. Trump that IEEPA does not authorize tariffs; BEA records the resulting refunds (about $166 billion excluding interest) as a capital transfer from the federal government in 2026Q1, NOT as a reduction of customs duties (BEA FAQ 1488, https://www.bea.gov/help/faq/1488), so the NIPA duties here are gross of refunds. Cash collections net of refunds are in treasuryMTS below. USITC calendar-year ratio of calculated duties to imports for consumption (the classic historical series) is in usitcRatio for 1947-2010 as a cross-check."
}